# host/guests.conf — the guest table (D-028, docs/MULTI_GUEST.md). Machine-specific: copy this file to
# guests.conf, fill it in, run ./install_guests.py. One line per guest, one emulator per machine.
#
# name      daemon  control  ssh                       emulator bundle (on that machine; may contain spaces)
#   name     = NAME= in that guest's AppleBridge Prefs; 1-31 of A-Z a-z 0-9 _ -
#   daemon   = TCPPORT= in that guest's prefs (9000 for a guest without the key)
#   control  = the port Claude, MCP and the watchdogs talk to (9001 keeps the single-guest names)
#   ssh      = - for the guest on this Mac, user@host for a guest on another Mac
# Convention: guest k gets 9000+10k / 9001+10k.
#
#dev       9000    9001     -                         /Users/you/Documents/Basilisk/BasiliskII.app
#second    9010    9011     you@192.0.2.20            /Users/you/Documents/BasiliskII/BasiliskII.app
